      "kind": "class",
      "doc": {
        "summary": "A capture target and its optional system authorization session.",
        "details": "Sources are shared identity objects, not persistent permission tokens. A source accepts only one in-flight screenshot or recording. Destroying the last reference releases its authorization resources. A disappearing target is never replaced. Factories only describe targets; permission may be requested during capture. Obtain other applications' windows through ScreenCapturer::SelectSource().\n\n```cpp\nauto source = CaptureSource::FromDisplay(DisplayManager::GetInstance().GetPrimary());\n```",
        "notes": [
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "text": "Platform availability:\n- macOS: ⚠️ ScreenCaptureKit on macOS 14+; system permission required\n- Windows: ⚠️ Windows Graphics Capture on Windows 10 2004+; desktop session required\n- Linux: ❌ Not implemented - Factories return nullptr\n- Android: ❌ Not implemented - Factories return nullptr\n- iOS: ❌ Not implemented - Factories return nullptr\n- OpenHarmony: ❌ Not implemented - Factories return nullptr"
          }
        ]
